sequenceDiagram
    %% PawPal+ AI planner — the agentic workflow: plan -> act -> check -> fix.
    %% Note who executes what: the model *requests* a tool, plan_day executes it
    %% locally against the real scheduler, and the result goes back to the model.
    %% The scheduler makes every placement decision. The model decides what to
    %% schedule and how to repair a plan the scheduler calls broken.
    %% Keep message text free of semicolons — mermaid reads ";" as the end of a
    %% statement, so the rest of the line is parsed as new syntax and fails.
    %% A bare "%%" line with no text after it is also a parse error here.

    actor User as Pet owner
    participant UI as Streamlit app.py
    participant Runner as plan_day tool loop
    participant Model as Gemini 3.6 Flash
    participant KB as knowledge/ care notes
    participant Sched as Owner / Schedule

    User->>UI: "Set up a daily routine for Mochi.<br/>I'm at work 09:00-17:00."
    UI->>Runner: plan_day(owner, request)
    Runner->>Model: request + tool definitions + system prompt

    Note over Model,Sched: PLAN — look at the day as it actually is
    Model->>Runner: show_current_state()
    Runner->>Sched: read pets, tasks, commitments
    Sched-->>Runner: current state
    Runner-->>Model: Mochi, dog, Shiba Inu, high energy

    Note over Model,KB: RETRIEVE — ground the routine before inventing it
    Model->>Runner: lookup_care_guidance, dog, high energy
    Runner->>KB: score 36 chunks, take top 3
    KB-->>Runner: dog_high_energy.md, breed_shiba_inu.md
    Runner-->>Model: 60-90 min daily, split across two walks

    Note over Model,Sched: ACT — add the retrieved tasks, then schedule them
    Model->>Runner: add_care_task(...) / add_commitment(...)
    Runner->>Sched: Pet.add_task() / Owner.add_commitment()
    Sched-->>Runner: confirmation or overlap warning
    Runner-->>Model: tool result

    loop up to MAX_REPAIR_ROUNDS, currently 3
        Model->>Runner: build_plan()
        Runner->>Sched: Owner.build_day()
        Sched-->>Runner: Schedule.explain()
        Runner-->>Model: the plan

        Note over Model,Sched: CHECK — the scheduler's own verdict
        Model->>Runner: review_plan()
        Runner->>Sched: detect_conflicts + unplaced + open gaps
        Sched-->>Runner: problems, or OK
        Runner-->>Model: verdict

        alt problems reported
            Note over Model,Sched: FIX — move or shorten, then rebuild
            Model->>Runner: retime_task() / resize_task()
            Runner->>Sched: update Task.scheduled_time or duration_minutes
            Sched-->>Runner: confirmation
            Runner-->>Model: tool result
        else no conflicts, nothing unplaced
            Note over Model: done repairing — leave the loop
        end
    end

    Model-->>Runner: what was scheduled, what moved, what didn't fit,<br/>and the notes it was based on
    Runner-->>UI: AgentResult(reply, actions)
    UI-->>User: answer plus step log, tables redraw from the mutated owner
